// Package eng is the engine: the entry into code compiled at run time and the
// PASM templates words are made of, in eng.spin2, whose comments give the
// registers, the stacks and the trap.
//
// The engine's state is in registers and LUT RAM of the cog that runs it, so
// a program runs words on one cog only, the one that calls Run, and the
// accessors here read that cog's registers.

// Run runs the code at xt until it returns or traps and answers the clocks
// it took. fresh is 1 to start a word and 0 to resume a trap's continuation.
func Run(xt, fresh uint32) uint32

// Start runs the code at xt on a free cog with par in PTRA and answers the
// cog, or -1.
func Start(xt, par uint32) int32

// Templates answers the hub address of the first template.
func Templates() uint32

// Refs answers the hub address of the instructions the encoder's test holds
// the compiler's output to, as flexspin assembled them.
func Refs() uint32

func SetTos(v uint32)
func GetTos() uint32
func SetDsp(v uint32)
func GetDsp() uint32
func SetRp(v uint32)
func GetRp() uint32
func GetPb() uint32
func SetPb(v uint32)

// Request answers a trap's request, 0 when the word returned.
func Request() uint32

// Continuation answers where a trapped word goes on.
func Continuation() uint32

// Layout answers the stacks' bounds: 0 for the data stack's base, 1 for its
// end, 2 for the empty return stack.
func Layout(i int32) uint32
